      * ZA0500 - allocate stock for order lines (JUCHUD) matched to
      * their order header (JUCHUM), M1/MR processing. Legacy system
      * (Part 5). JUCHUD is opened by JU0900C via OVRDBF SHARE(*YES);
      * this program only opens JUCHUM and ZAIKOM directly.
      * BUG (05-13 ticket 1): *ENTRY PLIST below declares MINQTY as
      * 5,0, but JU0900C declares the CL variable it passes as 3,0.
      * FIXED (found while writing za0510.rpg): the O-specs below
      * reference QSYSPRT, but this file had no FQSYSPRT F-spec line at
      * all - an undeclared file reference, which would fail to
      * compile. Added, matching ju0300.rpg's identical line.
      * FIXED (adversarial review, 2026-09-26): four more real bugs in
      * the C/O-specs below, found by re-deriving every line's opcode
      * semantics and column layout against RPG/400 Reference instead of
      * trusting the earlier hand-typed source. Regenerated via
      * tools/gen/rpg3.mjs's cSpec()/oSpec() rather than hand-edited.
      *   - CABEQ, not CASEQ: DOLIVE below is a TAG (GOTO target), not a
      *     BEGSR/ENDSR subroutine - CASxx's result field must name a
      *     subroutine and CASxx needs an ENDCS, neither of which applies
      *     here; CABxx's result field is a label, matching this GOTO/TAG
      *     idiom.
      *   - O-spec constants NOTFOUND/SHORT/OK now quoted with an end
      *     position (cols 40-43); the original bare, unquoted words with
      *     no end position would not compile (ju0300.rpg's OK/MISMATCH
      *     pair is the correct precedent, followed here).
      *   - No unconditional SETON LR: JUCHUD is the primary file (F-spec
      *     IP), so RPG/400 sets LR on automatically once it is
      *     exhausted. An unconditional SETON LR in detail calculations
      *     sets LR on the very first cycle, and the cycle does not read
      *     another primary record once LR is on - JU0900C calls ZA0500
      *     once and relies on ZA0500's own cycle to walk every matched
      *     order line, so this would have allocated stock for only the
      *     first line then returned.
      *   - Gated the allocation block on record-identifying indicator
      *     01 (JUCHUD's own turn) in addition to MR: a matched primary/
      *     secondary pair is processed as two separate detail cycles
      *     (rpg400ref.txt, matching-record Table 41), and MR stays on
      *     for both, so without the 01 gate the JUCHUM side of the same
      *     matched pair re-ran CHAIN/allocate/UPDAT/EXCPT against
      *     whatever JUSHO/JUSU were still sitting from the JUCHUD cycle
      *     (JUCHUM's own I-specs don't touch them), double-deducting
      *     stock and printing a duplicate line every time a match
      *     occurred.
     H
     FJUCHUD  IP  F      27            DISK
     FJUCHUM  IS  F      26            DISK
     FZAIKOM  UF  E           K        DISK
     FQSYSPRT O   F     132            PRINTER
     IJUCHUD      01
     I                                        1   6 JUNO    M1
     I                                        7   90JULINE
     I                                       10  15 JUSHO
     I                                       16  200JUSU
     I                                       21  272JUTNK
     IJUCHUM      02
     I                                        1   6 JUNO    M1
     I                                        7  12 JUTOK
     I                                       13  200JUDATE
     I                                       21  26 JUTAN
      * TICKET3 SOLUTION (05-13 checkpoint model answer, not the
      * as-shipped src/legacy/qrpgsrc/za0500.rpg): adds a program-wide
      * *PSSR that catches an unhandled runtime exception during detail
      * calculations (e.g. the SUB below, if fed corrupted JUSU data via
      * the 05-11 injection technique) and notifies the caller instead of
      * letting the job hang on an unanswered inquiry message (04-06/
      * 04-12's finding: unhandled severity-99 exception -> INQUIRY ->
      * indefinite hang in a non-interactive job).
      *
      * Scope judgment (ticket3's own hint: some errors are in *PSSR's
      * reach and some are not): this *PSSR is IN SCOPE for exceptions
      * raised during detail-calculation arithmetic (SUB/COMP/CHAIN with
      * no 56-57 indicator) - it is NOT in scope for OPEN/CLOSE-time
      * failures, which bypass INFSR *and* PSSR alike (RPG/400 Reference
      * p.38 lines 3127-3129, already cited in za0510.rpg's header note
      * 8; also matches docs/probes.md's 04-06 finding that *PSSR "did
      * not solve" an implicit-open failure). No per-file INFSR
      * continuation line is added here for that reason - only the
      * program-wide default-handler role (Chapter 2, Figure 7 step 3:
      * "the appropriate exception/error subroutine (INFSR or PSSR)",
      * already cited in za0510.rpg's header note 8) is relevant.
      *
      * FIXED (2026-09-26, real-hardware finding from part07-01-modules,
      * a different program, then redesigned here without a hardware
      * connection - column math checked with a script, not by hand;
      * still needs an actual CRTRPGPGM/CALL to confirm): this *PSSR used
      * to build a SNDPGMMSG MSGID(JUM0002) command and run it via CALL
      * 'QCMDEXC'. That is categorically broken from RPG - SNDPGMMSG
      * cannot run via QCMDEXC at all (registered MSGID or not), same
      * real-hardware finding as za0510.rpg's own *PSSR (CPD0031, see
      * that file's header for the full citation).
      *
      * NARRATIVE TRADE-OFF (flagged, not silently made): 05-13's own
      * lesson text (docs/part05/05-13-checkpoint-tickets.md) suggests
      * either "QCMDEXC-based SNDPGMMSG" or "a new JUMSGF message ID" -
      * but BOTH still need SOME transport to actually send a message,
      * and the only transport this repo has confirmed working from RPG
      * (QMHSNDPM, see jucutl.rpgle/f0605s.rpgle) needs new RPG III
      * fixed-form DS declarations (BINARY(4) fields for its length/
      * counter parameters) that have no precedent anywhere in this
      * repo's RPG III sources yet - deriving their exact column
      * positions from scratch, with no hardware connection to verify
      * them before the next commit, would be a second guess stacked on
      * top of this one. This solution instead reuses za0510.rpg's own
      * already-computed CHGDTAARA/*LDA replacement pattern (05-04),
      * trading the "registered JUMSGF message" flavor for one thing
      * that reuses an already-verified-safe command shape. If a future
      * connection confirms the QMHSNDPM/RPG III shape independently,
      * reconsider restoring the JUM0002 registered-message flavor here.
      *
      * QCMDEXC command text (RPG III cannot call a CL command directly -
      * ticket3's own hint): built via runtime MOVEL into CMDDS, same
      * technique and same reasoning as za0510.rpg's header note 9 (PARM
      * cannot take a DS with I-spec-initialized subfields, RPG/400
      * Reference p.318; each MOVEL chunk fits the C-spec Factor2 field's
      * 10-column width). CHGDTAARA DTAARA(*LDA (21 20)) VALUE('ZA0500
      * SHORT ERR') (56 characters, no padding needed - divides evenly
      * into 8 MOVEL chunks of 7 bytes) writes a fixed 20-byte flag into
      * bytes 21-40 of the job's own Local Data Area - a different byte
      * range from za0510.rpg's own *LDA use (bytes 1-20) so the two
      * programs' flags cannot collide if ever run in the same job,
      * though this is not expected to matter in practice. CHGDTAARA is
      * confirmed ALLOW(*ALL) on its own IBM Docs "Where allowed to run"
      * field - safe to run via QCMDEXC from any environment, unlike
      * SNDPGMMSG. No ADDMSGD/message-file setup is needed for this
      * solution any more (the JUM0002 message definition this file used
      * to require is no longer created or sent). The CALL itself
      * carries its own 56-57 error indicator (85, same convention
      * za0510.rpg uses on its own CALL 'QCMDEXC'): if QCMDEXC fails
      * while *PSSR is already running, this stops that failure from
      * re-invoking *PSSR (RPG/400 Reference p.38: "if an
      * exception/error occurs on the file already in error while the
      * subroutine is running, the subroutine is called again; this
      * will result in a program loop unless the programmer codes the
      * subroutine to avoid this problem").
     ICMDDS       DS                             56
     I                                        1   7 C1
     I                                        8  14 C2
     I                                       15  21 C3
     I                                       22  28 C4
     I                                       29  35 C5
     I                                       36  42 C6
     I                                       43  49 C7
     I                                       50  56 C8
     C           *ENTRY    PLIST
     C                     PARM           RMODE  10
     C                     PARM           MINQTY  50
     C   01 MR             GOTO PROCLN
     C                     GOTO SKPALL
     C           PROCLN    TAG
     C                     SETOF                     9091
     C           JUSHO     CHAINZAIKOM               90
     C  N90                Z-ADDZASU      AVAIL   70
     C  N90                SUB  JUSU      AVAIL
     C  N90      AVAIL     COMP MINQTY                 91
     C  N90N91   RMODE     CABEQ'*LIVE'   DOLIVE
     C                     GOTO SKPUPD
     C           DOLIVE    TAG
     C                     Z-ADDAVAIL     ZASU
     C                     UPDATZAIKOR
     C           SKPUPD    TAG
     C                     EXCPT
     C           SKPALL    TAG
      * *PSSR: see the header note above for scope/design.
     C           *PSSR     BEGSR
     C                     MOVEL'CHGDTAA' C1
     C                     MOVEL'RA DTAA' C2
     C                     MOVEL'RA(*LDA' C3
     C                     MOVEL' (21 20' C4
     C                     MOVEL')) VALU' C5
     C                     MOVEL'E(''ZA05'C6
     C                     MOVEL'00 SHOR' C7
     C                     MOVEL'T ERR'')'C8
     C                     Z-ADD56        CMDLEN 155
     C                     CALL 'QCMDEXC'              85
     C                     PARM           CMDDS
     C                     PARM           CMDLEN
     C                     ENDSR'*CANCL'
     OQSYSPRT E
     O                         JUNO       6
     O                         JUSHO     14
     O                         JUSU      21
     O                 90                30 'NOTFOUND'
     O                N90 91             30 'SHORT'
     O                N90N91             30 'OK'

